# The deployed artifact is site/dist and nothing else.
#
# Two reasons this file is not just tidiness. The harness talks to a paid API
# with a key read from the environment, and none of it -- not the client, not
# the config, not the cost guard -- belongs on a static host. And the repo root
# carries pyproject.toml, which is what made Vercel try to deploy src/tee/cli.py
# as a Python function in the first place; excluding it keeps the detection
# from having anything to find.
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
src/
tests/
configs/
corpora/
fixtures/
results/
.tee/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Site sources are built, not served. dist/ is what ships.
site/scripts/
site/content/
site/node_modules/

# site/vercel.json is read only when the project's Root Directory is `site`,
# in which case this file is not consulted at all. Harmless either way.
